-- === Math builtins ===
display absolute value of -42
display square root of 16
display floor of 3.7
display ceiling of 3.2
display 3.5 rounded
display 3.7 rounded down
display 3.2 rounded up

-- Power
display 2 to the power of 10
display 3 to power of 3

-- Min/max
display minimum of 5 and 10
display maximum of 5 and 10

-- Random (just check it doesn't crash)
r is random number between 1 and 100
display whether r is at least 1
display whether r is at most 100

-- === Type operations ===
display type of 42
display type of "hello"
display type of true
display type of [1, 2, 3]
display type of nothing

-- Type conversion
display "42" as a number
display 42 as a string
display convert "3.14" to number
display convert 100 to string
display convert true to a string

-- === Error handling ===
try
    display "Trying division by zero..."
    x is 10 / 0
catch error
    display "Caught: {error}".

-- Natural error handling
attempt
    raise "custom error"
if something goes wrong
    display "Handled it".

display "All stdlib tests passed"
